  "briefing": "Object Systems Regression. A is scale and footprints on the grid floor. B is selection: side by side, in front, behind a wide cover, on a tall platform, and through a hollow top. C is authored block heights 8, 16, 32, 64 and 92, including two- and three-high stacks (the prop stack cap is 3). D is tables, crates and platforms with small items on them. E is 92-tall calibration walls, a 46-tall wall, and items in front, behind and beside them. F is an open drop space with a few real inventory items. The south-east grid has a row of mock furniture along its north edge; the rest of it is empty.",
